## Retained attribute/option lifecycle
product-attributeLifecycle-title = Attribute and option lifecycle
product-attributeLifecycle-help = Edit exact-locale presentation, or archive and restore a retained definition. UUID, code, type, scope and SKU links are immutable. Archival is checked atomically by the owner; preview is advisory.
product-attributeLifecycle-directory = Active and archived attributes
product-attributeLifecycle-choose = Choose an attribute explicitly
product-attributeLifecycle-active = Active
product-attributeLifecycle-archived = Archived
product-attributeLifecycle-target = Definition to change
product-attributeLifecycle-attribute = Attribute presentation
product-attributeLifecycle-patch = Exact presentation JSON
product-attributeLifecycle-patchHelp = Only presentation fields are accepted, up to 8192 UTF-8 bytes. Missing translations stay null: no fallback text is copied. Omit a member to preserve it; identity, validation and defaults cannot be changed here. Position and search weight must be nonnegative when supplied. Reloading or changing the target replaces the unsent JSON draft. Only top-level omission preserves a member. A supplied translation object replaces the complete exact-locale copy; omitted nullable text members become null. A null translation does not delete an existing translation.
product-attributeLifecycle-locale = Exact locale:
product-attributeLifecycle-update = Save presentation
product-attributeLifecycle-archive = Archive without deleting IDs
product-attributeLifecycle-restore = Restore retained definition
product-attributeLifecycle-refresh = Reload definition and impact
product-attributeLifecycle-recover = Replay the exact saved request
product-attributeLifecycle-fresh = Open a fresh intent after this decision
product-attributeLifecycle-recoverStorage = Retry browser recovery
product-attributeLifecycle-stored = Inspect the complete saved request and decision
product-attributeLifecycle-unknown = The result is not confirmed. Only the exact saved body, original locale and key may be replayed, even if the directory cannot be loaded. Do not discard or retarget this request.
product-attributeLifecycle-confirmed = The owner confirmed this request. IDs and assignments were preserved. Open a fresh intent explicitly before another change; this result is not a Product revision.
product-attributeLifecycle-stale = The definition changed since it was read. This saved request was refused. Inspect it, then explicitly open a fresh intent and review the current definition before correcting the JSON.
product-attributeLifecycle-inUse = Archival was refused: retained values, bindings, axes or rules still reference this definition. Review the listed resources; nothing was silently detached or deleted.
product-attributeLifecycle-limit = Unused status could not be proved within the bounded inspection, or stored rules are malformed. Archival is refused. Resolve the retained schema data before a new explicit request.
product-attributeLifecycle-notFound = The selected definition is unavailable or no longer exists. Its saved IDs are retained for inspection; they are never replaced with the first available definition.
product-attributeLifecycle-parentArchived = Restore the parent attribute before restoring this option. The owner did not change either definition.
product-attributeLifecycle-invalid = Review the exact JSON: only mutable presentation members, a nonempty label and valid bounds are accepted. No replacement IDs or automatic corrections will be sent.
product-attributeLifecycle-storage = Browser recovery is unavailable or the authenticated scope changed. No new write is allowed. Restore this tab’s storage and original scope, then retry recovery; do not clear an unresolved request.
product-attributeLifecycle-selection = The attribute selection or recovery URL is invalid. Restore the original attribute_id/option_id and recovery marker instead of replacing an unresolved request.
product-attributeLifecycle-unavailable = The directory or impact is unavailable. Recovery remains independent of these reads. Lists are bounded to 1000 definitions/options; use the original selected definition rather than assuming an empty directory.
product-attributeLifecycle-impact = Retained references (bounded examples, not a total count)
product-attributeLifecycle-more = Additional references exist; the examples are not exhaustive.
